From 0a7b70cbcc0a9743487af7bceaf8d53aae2bc31d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: iasnezhkov <iasnezhkov@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 16:46:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] thermal: retry failed watched sensors without an infinite
 Looper wait

A due sensor returning ERROR or UNDER_COLLECTING skipped the sleep vote.
When all watched sensors failed, milliseconds::max narrowed to -1 in
Looper::pollOnce(int), allowing an indefinite wait for another event.
Retain the last successful severity, cooling request and timestamps,
retry at the existing 2000 ms minimum interval, and force an uncached
read after a dedicated retry deadline. Early thermal events neither
advance that deadline nor replace the failed sensor's cached sample.

Use the remaining interval for finite Looper waits, cap it at INT_MAX,
and reserve -1 for an actual idle watcher. Treat a healthy polling
interval boundary as due rather than returning a zero sleep vote.

Exact-source host regressions cover all-error/collecting retry, early
events, recovery, retained cooling, healthy cadence, finite timeout
narrowing and no-sensor idle. Android compilation and device recovery
from a sensor error remain separate integration checks.
